ui-options-tab-scp = SCP Options
ui-options-scp-graphics = Graphics
ui-options-scp-audio = Audio
ui-options-scp-game = Game
ui-options-tab-hover-to-see-details = Hover over an option to see a tooltip about what it does.
ui-options-fps-impact-attention =
    These settings directly affect game performance.
    Changing these settings will alter the FPS.
ui-options-grain-toggle-overlay = Use grain shader
ui-options-grain-toggle-overlay-tooltip =
    Whether to enable the grain shader.
    ATTENTION: The image will be overexposed in compatibility mode.
ui-options-grain-strength = Grain shader strength
ui-options-grain-strength-tooltip =
    Sets the intensity of the grain shader effects.
    The higher the value, the more "crackling" on screen.
ui-options-sin-city-toggle-overlay = Use Sin City shader
ui-options-sin-city-toggle-overlay-tooltip =
    Fully enables or disables the Sin City shader.
    Turn this off if the effect is distracting or you want the cleanest possible display.
ui-options-sin-city-strength = Sin City shader strength
ui-options-sin-city-strength-tooltip =
    Adjusts the Sin City shader intensity.
    A value of 100 preserves the current default appearance of the effect.
ui-options-field-of-view-blur-enabled = Field of view blur
ui-options-field-of-view-blur-enabled-tooltip =
    Blurs areas outside the field of view.
    Disable for better performance or if the effect is distracting.
ui-options-field-of-view-blur-scale = Field of view blur texture quality
ui-options-field-of-view-blur-scale-tooltip =
    Sets the quality of the blur texture. Higher values produce a more resource-intensive texture.
    ATTENTION: Can cause performance issues on weak video cards.
ui-options-field-of-view-opacity = Field of view opacity
ui-options-field-of-view-opacity-tooltip =
    Sets the opacity (darkness) of the space behind the character.
    The higher the value, the darker the space behind will be.
ui-options-light-bloom-enable = Bloom
ui-options-light-bloom-enable-tooltip =
    Determines whether the bloom effect will be used.
    On weak systems, enabling it may reduce performance.
ui-options-light-bloom-cone-enable = Bloom cone
ui-options-light-bloom-cone-enable-tooltip =
    Determines whether a cone is drawn from a light source.
    With it disabled, the light source will still have a small halo around it.
ui-options-light-bloom-cone-opacity = Bloom cone opacity
ui-options-light-bloom-cone-opacity-tooltip =
    Sets the opacity at which the bloom cone is drawn.
ui-options-light-bloom-optimizations = Reduced GPU load
ui-options-light-bloom-optimizations-tooltip =
    When enabled, light sources that are not visible to the character will not produce the effect.
    Visibility checks consume a large amount of CPU resources.
    This is likely to have the opposite effect unless your GPU is not weak.
    Recommended to use ONLY if your video card is VERY WEAK and you still want to play with the effect.
ui-options-light-bloom-strength = Bloom brightness
ui-options-light-bloom-strength-tooltip =
    Adjusts the brightness of the bloom effect. The higher the value, the brighter the bloom.
    Lets you tune the effect to your preferences.
ui-options-compatibility-mode-show-warning = Compatibility mode warning
ui-options-compatibility-mode-show-warning-tooltip =
    Determines whether you will receive a warning when compatibility mode is enabled each time you enter the game.
    Attention: For most players, following the warning instructions and disabling compatibility mode is recommended.
ui-options-compatibility-mode-use-shaders = Use shaders in compatibility mode
ui-options-compatibility-mode-use-shaders-tooltip =
    Allows shaders to run in compatibility mode despite graphic artifacts.
    Enable if you want to try playing this way.
ui-options-scp-typing-sound-enabled = Typing sounds
ui-options-scp-typing-sound-enabled-tooltip =
    When enabled, typing characters creates a distinct sound
ui-options-scp-typing-chat-submit-sound-enabled = Chat message send sounds
ui-options-scp-typing-chat-submit-sound-enabled-tooltip =
    When enabled, sending messages in the in-game chat creates a distinct sound
ui-options-scp-echo-enabled = Echo effect
ui-options-scp-echo-enabled-tooltip =
    When enabled, every non-global sound receives an echo effect.
    When enabled, all sounds may become louder. Use the volume slider to adjust the volume.
ui-options-scp-echo-strong-preset-preferred = Use strong echo effect
ui-options-scp-echo-strong-preset-preferred-tooltip =
    Determines whether a strong echo effect is used.
    In strong echo mode, sounds will have a longer tail.
ui-options-scp-audio-muffling-enabled = Sound muffling
ui-options-scp-audio-muffling-enabled-tooltip =
    Depending on the source position, it makes sound muffled or quieter.
    May cause performance issues on low-end systems.
ui-options-scp-game-auto-open-character-window-enabled = Auto-open character menu
ui-options-scp-game-auto-open-character-window-enabled-tooltip =
    Whether the character menu should automatically open when you join a new role.
    If you have not played this role before, the menu will show minimal information about your character and their role.
    On subsequent joins, the menu will stop opening.
